From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 15] amdgpu: the dpm performance level from /etc/system

Linux users force the power-management performance level by writing
"low", "high" or "auto" to the sysfs file power_dpm_force_performance_level
(amdgpu_set_power_dpm_force_performance_level()); illumos has no sysfs.
The illumos build gets a module variable, amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level
(0 auto = nothing forced, the default; 1 low; 2 high), set in
/etc/system like amdgpu's own parameters, and amdgpu_pci_probe() applies
it once, as the sysfs write does (amdgpu_dpm_force_performance_level()
under stable_pstate_ctx_lock), and logs the result.

Found on the Mac Pro 2013's compute GPU (Tahiti, legacy si_dpm,
2026-11-12): the driver switches to its balanced state at boot (four
levels, 300/150 to 725/1270 MHz) with the level "auto", but the SMC
stayed at level 0 under a full shader load; this is how to force the
top level, and to tell a stuck SMC from a wrong sensor.

License: a few lines in an MIT file; applied to the pinned Linux tree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -161,6 +161,15 @@
 int amdgpu_msi = -1;
 char amdgpu_lockup_timeout[AMDGPU_MAX_TIMEOUT_PARAM_LENGTH];
 int amdgpu_dpm = -1;
+#ifdef __illumos__
+/*
+ * illumos: the forced dpm performance level at probe, in place of Linux's
+ * sysfs power_dpm_force_performance_level (no sysfs here): 0 auto (the
+ * driver's default, nothing is forced), 1 low, 2 high. /etc/system:
+ * set amdgpu:amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level = 2
+ */
+int amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level = 0;
+#endif
 int amdgpu_fw_load_type = -1;
 int amdgpu_aspm = -1;
 int amdgpu_runtime_pm = -1;
@@ -2489,6 +2498,31 @@
 		drm_client_setup(adev_to_drm(adev), format);
 	}
 
+#ifdef __illumos__
+	/*
+	 * What writing power_dpm_force_performance_level does on Linux
+	 * (amdgpu_set_power_dpm_force_performance_level()), for the level
+	 * chosen in /etc/system; legacy and SMU dpm alike. Without dpm (or
+	 * with level 0) nothing changes.
+	 */
+	if (adev->pm.dpm_enabled && amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level != 0) {
+		enum amd_dpm_forced_level level =
+		    amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level == 1 ? AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_LOW :
+		    amdgpu_illumos_dpm_level == 2 ? AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_HIGH :
+		    AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_AUTO;
+		int r;
+
+		mutex_lock(&adev->pm.stable_pstate_ctx_lock);
+		r = amdgpu_dpm_force_performance_level(adev, level);
+		adev->pm.stable_pstate_ctx = NULL;
+		mutex_unlock(&adev->pm.stable_pstate_ctx_lock);
+		drm_info(adev_to_drm(adev),
+		    "illumos: dpm performance level %s (%d)\n",
+		    level == AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_LOW ? "low" :
+		    level == AMD_DPM_FORCED_LEVEL_HIGH ? "high" : "auto", r);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	ret = amdgpu_debugfs_init(adev);
 	if (ret)
 		DRM_ERROR("Creating debugfs files failed (%d).\n", ret);
